 - Any configuration change requires the recovery code, which unlocks a 10-minute session so it isn't asked for on every single action.
 
 
+## Schedules
+
+Config → **Schedules** lets you create recurring block windows (e.g. 22:00–06:00 on weekdays). While a window is open, Déchaîner:
+
+- **Suspends the selected apps** (Device Owner package suspension, so it works even if the accessibility service is off).
+- **Applies the selected services** (any Android user restriction, e.g. installing apps, Bluetooth, VPN config).
+- **Adds the selected websites** to the managed browser `URLBlocklist`, so the web version of a blocked app is blocked too.
+
+When the window closes, only what the schedule itself applied is released — manual suspensions and permanent restrictions are left alone. Windows repeat on the selected days until the schedule is disabled or deleted.
+
+Protection:
+
+- Editing, disabling or deleting a schedule requires the recovery code. Creating one or enabling one never does (it only adds blocking).
+- **Lock while active**: the schedule can't be changed at all while its window is open, not even with the recovery code.
+- **Lock date and time** (on by default): forces automatic time and blocks date/time settings while any schedule is enabled, so a window can't be skipped by changing the clock.
+- Enforcement runs from an exact alarm at every boundary, on boot, on clock/time-zone changes, on app update, and every 30s from the accessibility service. If a blocked app is reinstalled mid-window, it's sent back to the home screen and re-suspended.
+
 ## Installation and Configuration
 The elevation to Device Owner status requires a bridge between user-space and system-space. Follow these steps precisely:
 
